UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under GASB Statement No. 34, governmental fund financial statements report five fund types: General, Special Revenue, Debt Service, Capital Projects, and Permanent funds. These funds use the current financial resources measurement focus and modified accrual basis of accounting.
Wrong (B): Enterprise and internal service funds are proprietary funds, not governmental funds. They use the economic resources measurement focus and full accrual accounting.
Wrong (C): Pension trust, investment trust, custodial, and private-purpose trust funds are fiduciary fund types reported in separate fiduciary fund statements, not governmental fund statements.
