-- Q3240: State and Local Government Reporting [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under GASB Statement No. 68, each employer participating in a cost-sharing multiple-employer plan reports its proportionate share of the collective net pension liability on its government-wide financial statements. The proportion is typically based on the employer''s contributions relative to total employer contributions to the plan.
Wrong (A): GASB 68 requires recognition of a liability on the financial statements, not merely reporting contributions. Contribution-only reporting was the pre-GASB 68 approach.
Wrong (C): Each employer reports only its proportionate share, not the full plan liability. Reporting the entire liability would overstate a single employer''s obligation.
Wrong (D): The net pension liability is recognized on the face of the financial statements, not merely disclosed as a contingent liability in the notes.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3240;

-- Q3241: State and Local Government Reporting [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under GASB Statement No. 34, the government-wide statement of activities presents expenses by function or program, such as public safety, education, highways, and health. This functional format, combined with the net cost presentation, shows taxpayers the net cost of each government service.
Wrong (A): Natural classification (salaries, supplies, utilities) is used in governmental fund financial statements, not in the government-wide statement of activities.
Wrong (B): GASB 34 does not require a matrix format combining both natural and functional classification on the statement of activities.
Wrong (D): Alphabetical ordering by department name is not a presentation requirement under GASB standards for any financial statement.$EXPL$
