-- Q3242: State and Local Government Reporting [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 34, a grant restricted to building a library is classified as program revenue under capital grants and contributions on the statement of activities. It is specifically associated with the culture/recreation function and reduces the net cost of that program.
Wrong (A): General revenues include unrestricted resources such as property taxes and unrestricted grants. A grant restricted to a capital purpose is program revenue, not general revenue.
Wrong (B): Other financing sources is a governmental fund concept (e.g., bond proceeds, transfers) used in fund statements, not on the government-wide statement of activities.
Wrong (C): A restricted grant is recognized as revenue when eligibility requirements are met, not deferred as a liability until the library is built.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3242;

-- Q3243: State and Local Government Reporting [hard/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under GASB Statement No. 84, custodial funds report both a statement of fiduciary net position (assets and liabilities) and a statement of changes in fiduciary net position. This replaced the former agency fund model, which reported only assets and liabilities with no activity statement.
Wrong (A): Reporting only assets and liabilities with no fund balance was the old agency fund treatment under pre-GASB 84 standards. Custodial funds now report a full net position and changes statement.
Wrong (B): Custodial funds report fiduciary net position, not the three net position categories (net investment in capital assets, restricted, unrestricted) used in government-wide statements.
Wrong (C): Fiduciary funds do not report revenue and expenditures. They report additions and deductions on the statement of changes in fiduciary net position.$EXPL$
