  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 842-10-55-22, the lease term includes the noncancellable period plus any periods covered by renewal options that the lessee is reasonably certain to exercise. Since the lessee is reasonably certain to exercise the 5-year renewal, the lease term is 10 + 5 = 15 years.
Wrong (A): Ten years reflects only the initial noncancellable period and ignores the renewal option the lessee is reasonably certain to exercise.
Wrong (B): Five years represents only the renewal period. The lease term must include both the initial noncancellable period and the reasonably certain renewal.
Wrong (D): ASC 842 does not apply a "shorter of" test to the lease term. When renewal is reasonably certain, the full combined period is used.$EXPL$
