-- Q3278: Advanced Lease Transactions [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 842-10-30-9, initial direct costs--those that would not have been incurred without obtaining the lease, such as broker commissions and certain legal fees--are included in the initial measurement of the ROU asset for both operating and finance leases.
Wrong (B): Initial direct costs are not expensed as incurred. They are capitalized into the ROU asset and recognized over the lease term through amortization.
Wrong (C): The capitalization of initial direct costs applies to both finance and operating leases equally. ASC 842 does not distinguish between classifications for this treatment.
Wrong (D): Initial direct costs are added to the ROU asset, not deducted from the lease liability. The lease liability reflects only the present value of lease payments.$EXPL$
