-- Q3279: Advanced Lease Transactions [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under ASC 842-20-25-5, a finance lease lessee separately recognizes amortization of the ROU asset (typically straight-line) and interest expense on the lease liability (effective interest method). Because interest is calculated on the declining liability balance, total expense is front-loaded--higher in early years and lower in later years.
Wrong (A): Straight-line lease expense applies to operating leases under ASC 842-20-25-6, not finance leases. Finance leases split expense into amortization and interest components.
Wrong (B): Variable lease expense based on usage is not the standard recognition pattern for either finance or operating leases. It applies only to certain variable payment arrangements.
Wrong (C): Cash-basis recognition of lease payments is not permitted under ASC 842. Both operating and finance leases require accrual-basis expense recognition.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3279;

