  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Variable lease payments based on sales are not one of the five finance lease classification criteria under ASC 842-10-25-2. Such payments are excluded from the lease liability and expensed as incurred. They do not affect lease classification.
Wrong (A): Ownership transfer at the end of the lease term is one of the five classification criteria. If met, the lease is classified as a finance lease.
Wrong (B): A lease term covering the major part of the remaining economic life of the underlying asset is a valid finance lease criterion under ASC 842-10-25-2.
Wrong (C): A present value of lease payments equaling or exceeding substantially all of the underlying asset''s fair value is a valid finance lease criterion under ASC 842-10-25-2.$EXPL$
